        "date": "2026-11-15T07:18:51Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): sinker body electrode - outline atom, tool record and electrode from faces\n\nA sinker electrode can be a body: a closed outline extruded along Z.\n\n- sim: stock_sim::simulate_outline burns the outline, grown by the spark\n  gap, along straight chords through the column grid. Exact at each\n  column centre (polygon inside joined with a stadium on each edge; a\n  chord meets a stadium in one interval, in closed form). Arcs, posed\n  moves, non-finite moves, a bad gap and an outline that is no section\n  are refused by name before a column is lowered. The box atom (#541)\n  is unchanged.\n- tools: Tool::outline (mm about the burn point; empty for a\n  rectangular face). diameter and width stay the outline's X and Y\n  extents. The record's door refuses an outline that is no simple\n  section (3 to 1024 points) and sizes that leave it.\n- motion: electrode_from_faces yields a body electrode for a cavity\n  that is no axis-aligned rectangle; the NON_RECTANGULAR refusal is\n  gone. The obstruction check uses the cavity's outline as the column.\n  The size law of #543 judges an outline on its extents.\n- app: the program verdict burns a record with an outline with the\n  outline atom. The outline goes through the project file, the library,\n  the MCP tool definitions and the operation stamp. The field eye still\n  refuses an electrode (#548).\n- ui: the tool draft carries the outline through an Apply.\n\nDecisions: docs/decisions/1152-electrode-body.md. Synthetic conditions\nonly; not exercised on a real EDM control.\n\nFixes #1152\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
